# (MiMa against every release in `Versions.binaryCompatBaselines`, build.mill). CONTRIBUTING.md,
# "Binary compatibility", says when a line belongs here and when the old signature must stay.
#
# One finding per line, with the two names exactly as the check prints them and a reason:
#
#   <ProblemType> <member>  # <reason>
#
# A line without a reason fails the check. So does a line that matches no finding.

# --- Hidden forwarders: these link. They are not breaks. ---
#
# Each member below was public in 1.0.x and is now a `private[fastmcp]` forwarder with the same JVM
# signature. That is public in bytecode, so a program compiled against 1.0.x links and runs; new
# source cannot call it. MiMa reports `MethodNoLongerCheckedProblem` because it skips a member that
# is package-private in the baseline: a comparison against 1.1.0 alone would not notice the
# forwarder being removed. Two things do notice: 1.0.0 and 1.0.1 stay in `binaryCompatBaselines`,
# where the signatures are public, and `BinaryCompatibilityTest` calls every one of them by its old
# signature.
